### 6. Business Insights & Recommendations

## Key Insights

* Customers with an International Plan experienced higher churn than customers without one.
* Frequent customer service calls were associated with increased churn, suggesting unresolved service issues.
* Heavy day-time usage customers showed different churn behavior compared to customers with lower usage.
* Customer retention varied across states, indicating regional differences.
* Customers with longer account tenure generally demonstrated stronger loyalty.

---

## Recommendations

* Proactively engage customers who make multiple customer service calls.
* Improve support quality and reduce issue resolution time.
* Develop personalized retention campaigns for high-risk customer segments.
* Monitor customers enrolled in international plans for early churn signals.
* Strengthen loyalty initiatives for long-term customers.

